  "instructions": [
    "Heat the beurre noisette in a large molcajete vessel over medium heat.",
    "Add the chopped onion and cook until softened, about 5 minutes.",
    "Add the minced garlic and grated ginger and cook for an additional 1 minute.",
    "Stir in the cumin, coriander, cayenne pepper, salt, and black pepper.",
    "Add the red lentils, chopped pickle, and vegetable broth to the molcajete vessel.",
    "Bring the mixture to a boil, then reduce the heat to low and simmer, covered, for 20 minutes.",
    "Remove the lid and continue to simmer, uncovered, for an additional 10 minutes, or until the lentils are tender.",
    "Serve the warm spicy Saudi Arabian lentil tagine hot, garnished with chopped fresh herbs if desired."
